(memory "llm/extract" :when "the agent holds a text, page, comment or mail and must pull fields or structured data out of it")
llm/extract shape: alist of (key . field), written by (shape (name spec...) ...)
: no quote, no dotted pairs. Field is:
  :string, :number, :integer, :boolean, :any; plain string = string field
  described by its text;
  (:string "what it means") and same for other scalars;
  (:enum "a" "b") ; (:list field) ; (:optional field) , only field model may
  omit; nested alist = nested object. Alist shape returns alist, (:list …)
  returns list. :instructions "..." says what to pull out.
  Nested group = nested object; (:list …) and (:optional …) take groups too:
(shape (items (:list (id :number) (title :string))))
  is list of objects. Shape is literal, built at compile time: computed enum
  needs hand-written alist.

(llm/extract page (shape (title "the page title")
    (stars :integer)
    (state (:enum "open" "closed"))
    (links (:list :string))
    (author (:optional (:string "who wrote it")))))
llm/extract-1: alist, keys "title" "stars" "state" "links"

Text arguments: prompt, :system, :instructions, llm/extract text, message
content. Any value works.

(memory "llm/complete" :when "the agent is about to send one prompt to a model, or several messages as one conversation, or a model call just failed")
- (llm/complete "prompt") waits, gives reply string. Prompt is any value: list or alist goes in printed, no (string …) needed.
- (llm/chat messages) gives reply string, multi-turn. Message is (message :system "...") or (message :user "...") . Bare string = user message.

(llm/complete "Name three risks in this plan" :system "Be blunt." :max-tokens 200)
llm/complete-1: 84 words

(llm/chat (list (message :system "Answer in one sentence.") (message :user q)))

Text arguments: prompt, :system, :instructions, llm/extract text, message
content. Any value works.

(memory "llm/macros" :when "the agent holds a long text or many records that must be summarized, or a question must be answered from a given text or data")
Three forms over llm/complete carry prompt for you; (doc 'summarize) and
expansion are all there is. Each takes llm/complete options plus :words,
capping asked length and token budget.

- (summarize value :words 60 [option...]) gives summary. Printed form goes in
  prompt, so list of records works like page of text.
- (summarize-each values :words 25 [option...]) gives summaries in order, one
  sequential call per element: slice with (head x 5) first, never hundreds.
- (llm/answer question context :words 60 [option...]) answers from context
  only. Not in context: nil, not a guess. nil never means failed call: branch
  on it, do not echo it.

(setq brief (summarize acme/list-issues-1 :words 40))
brief: 39 words

(echo brief)

(setq owner (llm/answer "who is assigned to ENG-12?" acme/list-issues-1))
owner: "Nadia"

(echo (if owner owner "the issues do not say who is assigned"))

(memory "llm/options" :when "a model call needs a particular model or provider, a timeout, or defaults changed for many calls, or a model call just timed out")
Options, all optional, every call: :provider, keyword from (llm/providers) ·
:model, string · :system · :max-tokens · :temperature · :reasoning-effort,
:low, :medium or :high · :timeout ms, default 60000.

(llm/providers) gives row per reachable provider, (provider default-model
status) , status :ready or :no-api-key. First row = default :provider.

Global *llm-defaults* = keyword list every call starts from; call-site option
wins. (with-llm (option...) body...) extends it for one block, restores after:

(with-llm (:provider :openrouter :max-tokens 120)
  (summarize-each (head pages-1 3)))
